00:15:23.188 --> 00:15:24.723
at any given moment?

00:15:24.723 --> 00:15:27.559
You do a little bit more of a
straight thing on "The Five",

00:15:27.559 --> 00:15:29.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you know, you're
yourself, but the show is

00:15:29.594 --> 00:15:32.130 align:start size:84% position:16%
a little more
straight or narrow.

00:15:32.130 --> 00:15:37.202
- It's weird because
what the irony is,

00:15:38.469 --> 00:15:42.140 align:start size:97% position:3%
more dangerous on "Gutfeld",
they leave me alone,

00:15:42.140 --> 00:15:45.377
but the people that are
really trying to get me

00:15:45.377 --> 00:15:50.315
are the ones that are
auditing "The Five".

00:15:50.315 --> 00:15:54.252 align:start size:97% position:3%
So it's like they're not
taking the course, you know.

00:15:54.252 --> 00:15:56.521
They're showing up
in the back hoping

00:15:56.521 --> 00:15:59.591 align:start size:88% position:13%
that the professor
uses the wrong pronoun.

00:15:59.591 --> 00:16:01.960
That's what I notice
that it's more like.

00:16:01.960 --> 00:16:07.032
So you know, I would assume
that at least once a week

00:16:08.400 --> 00:16:12.337
there is somebody deliberately
trying to destroy my career,

00:16:12.337 --> 00:16:14.405
but I can't let that stop me.

00:16:14.405 --> 00:16:18.277 align:start size:97% position:3%
I have to, I've talked about
this in previous books.

00:16:18.277 --> 00:16:20.011
We all have to share the risk.

00:16:20.011 --> 00:16:23.448
And I have to always, I'm not
blowing smoke up your ass,

00:16:23.448 --> 00:16:27.486
but I have to say that you
helped destroy cancel culture

00:16:27.486 --> 00:16:31.489
by monetizing the act
of being canceled.

00:16:31.489 --> 00:16:35.294
If you get canceled and
there's another way out,

00:16:35.294 --> 00:16:37.161
you will always rise above.

00:16:37.161 --> 00:16:41.366 align:start size:97% position:3%
The perfect example is Jason
Aldean getting targeted,

00:16:41.366 --> 00:16:43.102
his song goes to number one.

00:16:43.102 --> 00:16:44.336
There are a lot of other things.

00:16:44.336 --> 00:16:47.171 align:start size:88% position:13%
And then there's the
reverse, that if you try

00:16:47.171 --> 00:16:51.143 align:start size:97% position:3%
to be the opposite of cancel
culture, that is, woke,

00:16:51.143 --> 00:16:53.945
that will have an effect,
like the Bud Light thing

00:16:53.945 --> 00:16:57.549
where that is actually
people, not social media,

00:16:57.549 --> 00:16:59.051
but people going,
"Do you know what?

00:16:59.051 --> 00:17:00.919
I don't like that they're
trying to sell me something

00:17:00.919 --> 00:17:02.321
that's so fake."

00:17:02.321 --> 00:17:05.858 align:start size:97% position:3%
And by the way, the
